# StudentStack — Cursor Rules (strict)

## Brand & UI/UX
- Visual language: extreme modern roundness (large border radii), bubbly rounded sans-serif typography, soft and vibrant pastels, thick drop shadows, playful bouncy hover animations (reference: Duolingo, Kalshi energy).
- Interactions: prefer `motion` / CSS transitions with subtle scale and shadow on hover; avoid flat static panels without feedback.

## Icons
- Never use generic placeholder icons, emoji-as-icons for UI chrome, or “AI JSON” / stock robot icons.
- Use **Lucide React** (or other curated SVG icon libraries) or intentional **CSS shapes** only.

## Product & Content Boundaries
- **Primary monetization:** StudentStack Daily membership (**$40/mo**). CTA says “Join the daily”; reveal price only after that step.
- Public surface also includes **partner certifications**. No student login on the marketing site.
- Present as a **student-led organization**. Do not market “AI writes the newsletter” on the public site; the operator engine may use AI internally.
- Operator portal at `/operator` (default credentials `admin` / `admin` unless env overrides).
- Do not advertise Elite portal / 24/7 concierge as the lead CTA.

## Engineering defaults
- App is Next.js at the repo root under `src/`. Prefer extending `/operator` and `/api/admin/*` / `/api/cron/*` for the newsletter engine.
